      "math_academy_id": "q-80399",
      "sequence_position": 1,
      "problem": "For the function $f(x,y),$ calculate $\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y}$ given that $\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=-\\frac{xy}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}.$",
      "worked_solution": "To find $\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y}$ we differentiate the given first-order partial derivative $\\frac{∂f}{∂y}$ with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\frac{∂f}{∂y}) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(-\\frac{xy}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}) \\\\  & =-y\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\frac{x}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}) \\\\  & =-y(\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}-\\frac{2{x}^{2}}{({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})^{2}}) \\\\  & =-y(\\frac{({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})-2{x}^{2}}{({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})^{2}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{y({x}^{2}-{y}^{2})}{({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
